<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110767" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐάλλω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐᾰλῶ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>undertake, take in hand, set
				about</i> a thing, found twice in codd. of <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲ φιαλεῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>V.</u>
					1348
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅπως ἔργῳ φιαλοῦμεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Pax</u>
					432
				</span></i>
			: acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1403.16
			</span></i> it is shortd. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφιάλλω;</span>
			hence Bentley restored <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽
			ἐφιαλεῖς</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔργῳ
			᾽φιαλοῦμεν.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
